    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1293">

                <pb facs="1242" n="1076" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1076"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/322</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Collector Cobb to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-05T18:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 5, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Francisco Murguia is back in Chihuahua. Americans affected by general
                    loan inclined to wait and see what he will do before asking assistance of
                    Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cobb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
